l folders holding one link per entry), the broken links into the Skilled checkout that the plan replaces or removes, and the ignore lines in <git-dir>/info/exclude (or .gitignore behind --ignore gitignore), with the run record written to the checkout's .skilled/output/doctor-symlink/<first 16 hex of the digest>/manifest.json, or the next free <prefix>-2, <prefix>-3 folder when an earlier run holds it, before the first action; no real file or folder is ever overwritten, and the write runs only against the plan digest the operator approved\"\n578-    mcp_tools: []   # script-only; no MCP calls\n579-    script_invocations:\n580-      - 'node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/symlink-engine.cjs plan --root <dir>  # read-only: prints every action, every refusal and the plan digest; the workflow adds --runtimes, --mode, --include, --link-instructions and --ignore only when the operator passed them'\n581-      - 'node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/symlink-engine.cjs apply --root <dir> --plan-digest <digest>  # recomposes with the same flags, refuses a digest that no longer matches, records the run, applies the actions and reruns check; the workflow runs it only after the operator approves the plan that printed that digest'\n582-    trigger_phrases:\n583-      - \"symlink skilled into my project\"\n584-      - \"link the claude folder into my repo\"\n585-      - \"repair broken skilled symlinks\"\n586-      - \"create the skilled links in a repo\"\n587-      - \"link skilled into my repo\"\n588-      - \"link skilled into another project\"\n589-      - \"link my skilled checkout into another project\"\n590-\n591:  - command: /doctor:symlink\n592-    target: unlink\n593-    yaml: doctor-symlink-unlink.yaml\n594-    setup_vars: [execution_mode, run_dir, yes, dry_run]\n595-    allowed_flags: [\"--run <dir>\", \"--yes\", \"--dry-run\"]\n596-    mutating: mutates\n597-    gate3_location: \"only the links, the folders and the ignore lines one run's manifest.json records, each r