{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794528291444,"sessionID":"ses_e2dcb1a37ffeB0Y69siDRonAev","part":{"partID":"prt_1d238a7b1001VxefNp44ryXWNk","sessionID":"ses_e2dcb1a37ffeB0Y69siDRonAev","messageID":"msg_1d2388bb8001fwWOaDQj7CLpMy","type":"tool","id":"call_b5a2f51de362448e8813cd33","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-symlink-check.yaml","offset":20,"limit":50},"output":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-symlink-check.yaml, lines 20-69\n20: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n21: # MUTATION BOUNDARIES (READ-ONLY)\n22: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n23: mutation_boundaries:\n24:   read_only: true\n25:   allowed_targets: []\n26:   forbidden_targets:\n27:     - \"**/*\"\n28:   invariant: \"This route runs the check subcommand only. It never runs plan, apply or unlink, and it never writes a link, directory, ignore line or run record. Findings describe the target repository and do not change its state. The route also runs the read-only hook-wiring check, which reads each installed runtime's prompt hook entry and never writes.\"\n29: \n30: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n31: # UPSTREAM ASSETS\n32: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n33: upstream_assets:\n34:   engine: \".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/symlink-engine.cjs\"\n35:   manifest: \".skilled/commands/doctor/assets/symlink-manifest.json\"\n36:   presentation: \".skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-symlink-presentation.txt\"\n37:   hook_wiring: \".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs\"\n38: \n39: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n40: # INPUTS\n41: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n42: inputs:\n43:   execution_mode: \"INTERACTIVE\"\n44:   root: \"Required target project repository, passed as --root <dir>. The engine requires it to exist and be a directory.\"\n45:   runtimes: \"Optional comma-separated runtime names, passed as --runtimes <list> when supplied: claude,opencode,codex,cursor,devin,pi. When omitted, the engine selects runtimes whose primary entry already exists in the target root. The core entry is always included.\"\n46:   include: \"Optional comma-separated extras, passed as --include <list> when supplied: repo-rules,github,utcp,env.\"\n47:   link_instructions: \"When true, pass --link-instructions to include AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md and REPO RULES.md.\"\n48:   json_output: \"When true, pass --json and show only the engine's JSON object. The default is false.\"\n49:   target: \"The route accepts the check action. A missing --root value or any unsupported flag is refused by the engine.\"\n50: \n51: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n52: # EXECUTION\n53: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n54: execution:\n55:   steps:\n56:     - \"Check that .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/symlink-engine.cjs, .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/symlink-manifest.json and .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-symlink-presentation.txt exist. If one is missing, report its path and stop with STATUS=FAIL. Do not create the presentation file here.\"\n57:     - 'Run node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/symlink-engine.cjs check --root \"{root}\", adding --runtimes \"{runtimes}\" when supplied, --include \"{include}\" when supplied, --link-instructions when requested and --json when requested.'\n58:     - \"The engine reports one status for each selected manifest entry, with detail lines for missing children, broken links and local conflicts. It also reports detected runtimes, tracked absolute links, Git state and applicable warnings.\"\n59:     - \"Exit 0 means no drift was found. Exit 1 means drift was found: broken links, foreign links, broken links inside merged folders, a missing source, or tracked absolute links. Missing children in a partial merge do not count as drift. Show the report and end with STATUS=WARN. Exit 2 means the invocation or target root was refused. Quote the engine message and end with STATUS=FAIL.\"\n60:     - 'After the engine report, run node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs --root \"{root}\" to read the prompt hook entry each installed runtime loads. It skips a runtime whose folder is absent. Show every hook-missing <runtime> line as printed. Exit 0 leaves the status unchanged. Exit 1 ends the run with STATUS=WARN and names the repair: copy the prompt hook entry from the matching file in the Skilled checkout into the target file for that runtime. Exit 2 means the check was refused: quote its message and end with STATUS=FAIL.'\n61:     - \"Render the engine output through .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-symlink-presentation.txt. When --json was requested, print the engine's JSON object alone.\"\n62: \n63: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n64: # OUTPUT\n65: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n66: output: |\n67:   STATUS=OK when the engine exits 0. Show the check report through the presentation contract.\n68:   STATUS=WARN when the engine exits 1. Show the check report through the presentation contract.\n69:   STATUS=FAIL when the engine exits 2 or cannot run. Name the accepted invocation (/doctor:symlink check --root <dir> [flags]) and quote the engine message.","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-symlink-check.yaml, lines 20-69\n20: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n21: # MUTATION BOUNDARIES (READ-ONLY)\n22: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n23: mutation_boundaries:\n24:   read_only: true\n25:   allowed_targets: []\n26:   forbidden_targets:\n27:     - \"**/*\"\n28:   invariant: \"This route runs the check subcommand only. It never runs plan, apply or unlink, and it never writes a link, directory, ignore line or run record. Findings describe the target repository and do not change its state. The route also runs the read-only hook-wiring check, which reads each installed runtime's prompt hook entry and never writes.\"\n29: \n30: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n31: # UPSTREAM ASSETS\n32: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n33: upstream_assets:\n34:   engine: \".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/symlink-engine.cjs\"\n35:   manifest: \".skilled/commands/doctor/assets/symlink-manifest.json\"\n36:   presentation: \".skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-symlink-presentation.txt\"\n37:   hook_wiring: \".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs\"\n38: \n39: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n40: # INPUTS\n41: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n42: inputs:\n43:   execution_mode: \"INTERACTIVE\"\n44:   root: \"Required target project repository, passed as --root <dir>. The engine requires it to exist and be a directory.\"\n45:   runtimes: \"Optional comma-separated runtime names, passed as --runtimes <list> when supplied: claude,opencode,codex,cursor,devin,pi. When omitted, the engine selects runtimes whose primary entry already exists in the target root. The core entry is always included.\"\n46:   include: \"Optional comma-separated extras, passed as --include <list> when supplied: repo-rules,github,utcp,env.\"\n47:   link_instructions: \"When true, pass --link-instructions to include AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md and REPO RULES.md.\"\n48:   json_output: \"When true, pass --json and show only the engine's JSON object. The default is false.\"\n49:   target: \"The route accepts the check action. A missing --root value or any unsupported flag is refused by the engine.\"\n50: \n51: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n52: # EXECUTION\n53: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n54: execution:\n55:   steps:\n56:     - \"Check that .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/symlink-engine.cjs, .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/symlink-manifest.json and .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-symlink-presentation.txt exist. If one is missing, report its path and stop with STATUS=FAIL. Do not create the presentation file here.\"\n57:     - 'Run node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/symlink-engine.cjs check --root \"{root}\", adding --runtimes \"{runtimes}\" when supplied, --include \"{include}\" when supplied, --link-instructions when requested and --json when requested.'\n58:     - \"The engine reports one status for each selected manifest entry, with detail lines for missing children, broken links and local conflicts. It also reports detected runtimes, tracked absolute links, Git state and applicable warnings.\"\n59:     - \"Exit 0 means no drift was found. Exit 1 means drift was found: broken links, foreign links, broken links inside merged folders, a missing source, or tracked absolute links. Missing children in a partial merge do not count as drift. Show the report and end with STATUS=WARN. Exit 2 means the invocation or target root was refused. Quote the engine message and end with STATUS=FAIL.\"\n60:     - 'After the engine report, run node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs --root \"{root}\" to read the prompt hook entry each installed runtime loads. It skips a runtime whose folder is absent. Show every hook-missing <runtime> line as printed. Exit 0 leaves the status unchanged. Exit 1 ends the run with STATUS=WARN and names the repair: copy the prompt hook entry from the matching file in the Skilled checkout into the target file for that runtime. Exit 2 means the check was refused: quote its message and end with STATUS=FAIL.'\n61:     - \"Render the engine output through .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-symlink-presentation.txt. When --json was requested, print the engine's JSON object alone.\"\n62: \n63: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n64: # OUTPUT\n65: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n66: output: |\n67:   STATUS=OK when the engine exits 0. Show the check report through the presentation contract.\n68:   STATUS=WARN when the engine exits 1. Show the check report through the presentation contract.\n69:   STATUS=FAIL when the engine exits 2 or cannot run. Name the accepted invocation (/doctor:symlink check --root <dir> [flags]) and quote the engine message."}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-symlink-check.yaml\",\"offset\":20,\"limit\":50}"},"time":{"start":1794528290737,"end":1794528291444}}}}
