{"type":"text","timestamp":1794528325024,"sessionID":"ses_e2dcb1a37ffeB0Y69siDRonAev","part":{"id":"prt_1d23922f0002KNP11FBGwa2320","sessionID":"ses_e2dcb1a37ffeB0Y69siDRonAev","messageID":"msg_1d2390b50001Oy0UJyUB0HWati","type":"text","text":"T015 is done. `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-symlink-check.yaml` now declares the hook-wiring check and keeps its contract green.\n\nChanges in that file only:\n\n1. Added `hook_wiring: \".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs\"` to `upstream_assets`.\n2. Added an execution step after the engine report that runs `node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs --root \"{root}\"`, shows each `hook-missing <runtime>` line, sets `STATUS=WARN` on exit 1 and names the repair, with exit 0 leaving the status unchanged and exit 2 ending as `STATUS=FAIL`.\n3. Appended to the invariant that the route also runs the read-only hook-wiring check, keeping `check subcommand only`.\n\nVerify output:\n\n```\n$ rg -c \"hook-wiring-check.cjs\" .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-symlink-check.yaml\n2\n(rg exit: 0)\n\n$ node --test .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/doctor-symlink-contract.test.cjs .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/doctor-runtime-mirrors-contract.test.cjs\n...\nℹ tests 43\nℹ pass 43\nℹ fail 0\n```\n\nBaseline before the edit was `rg -c` with no match (exit 1) and DCT at 43 pass, 0 fail. The scoped diff is 3 insertions and 1 deletion in the one named file. I did not tick the T015 checkbox, edit any other file or touch git state.\n\nNothing was blocked. The T015 checkbox remains for the orchestrator to tick.","time":{"start":1794528322288,"end":1794528325024}}}
